  "answer":"No. The current production checklist does not allow a release based solely on accuracy > 0.80. The release policy requires evaluation on a frozen holdout and promotion only when F1 improves by at least 0.005 and ROC‑AUC does not drop by more than 0.01. The older rule that any model with accuracy > 0.80 could be promoted has been superseded by this policy.",
  "sources":[
    {
      "source_id":"release-policy",
      "quote":"Production model changes require an evaluation on a frozen holdout. Promote only when F1 improves by at least 0.005 and ROC-AUC drops by no more than 0.01."
    },
    {
      "source_id":"legacy-policy",
      "quote":"The old 2024 process promoted any model when accuracy exceeded 0.80. It is superseded by release-policy: current releases use F1 and ROC-AUC on a frozen holdout."
    }
  ]
}
